Three changes to `ChooseYourPathScene.cs`:

**Fix (a) — Class blurb no longer clipped**
- `textBlock.SizeFlagsVertical` changed from `4` (ShrinkCenter) to `3` (Fill|Expand) so it claims a share of the panel's vertical space alongside the portrait instead of taking only its (underreported) minimum height.
- `SizeFlagsStretchRatio = 0.10f` keeps the portrait dominant (~91% of extra space) while giving the text block enough room for all wrapped text.
- Removed `ClipContents = true` from the panel as a safety net — labels with Autowrap can report a minimum height lower than their actual laid-out height; without ClipContents, any overflow stays visible within the carousel clip container.

**Fix (b) — Carousel dots are no longer obscured by BEGIN button**
- Dot area raised from `sectionH - 32` to `sectionH - 52` (20px higher).
- Dot area height reduced from 26px to 20px.
- This creates a clear visual separation between the position dots and the BEGIN button below the carousel.

